@startuml SmartLost_Matching_Sequence
title SmartLost - UML Matching Sequence\nUC08 View matching suggestions\nProposed semester integration - not implemented
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 65

actor "Registered User\nLost Item Owner or Finder" as User
boundary "Angular Web App" as Web
control "Listings Service\nAPI and Listing Queries" as Listings
box "Matching Service - one proposed application process" #EFF6FF
  control "Suggestion Coordinator\nvia internal Matching API" as Matching
  control "Candidate Selector" as Selector
  control "Relevance Ranker" as Ranker
  participant "Embedding Service\nDINOv3 adapter and versioned cache" as Embeddings
end box
database "Matching Database\nSearch projections and embeddings" as DB

note over Listings, DB
  Listings is authoritative for listing state, decisions and recoveries.
  Durable retryable updates populate Matching projections separately.
  Duplicate/older change sequences must not overwrite newer state.
  This query does not publish a listing or execute a recovery.
end note

User -> Web : Open suggestions for an owned Open listing
Web -> Listings : Request suggestions for listing
Listings -> Listings : Validate token, ownership, current revision\nand source listing eligibility
alt Unauthorised, not owned or ineligible source
  Listings --> Web : Access error or current unavailable/conflict outcome
  Web --> User : Show error or current listing state
else Authorised and eligible source
  Listings -> Matching : Request suggestions for listing identifier\nand expected source revision
  alt Matching unreachable or request times out
    Listings -> Listings : Observe call failure or timeout\nPreserve the published listing
    Listings --> Web : Explicit unavailable processing outcome
    Web --> User : Show that suggestions are unavailable\nAllow a later retry
  else Matching request handled
    Matching -> DB : Read source projection, revision\nand processing/eligibility state
    DB --> Matching : Projection and status, or no current projection
    alt Source projection missing, stale or processing failed
      Matching -> Matching : Prepare explicit pending/failed outcome\nDo not label stale results as ready
    else Projection current but source no longer eligible
      Matching -> Matching : Prepare unavailable/current-state outcome
    else Current eligible projection
      Matching -> Selector : Select candidate pool for this source
      Selector -> DB : Query Open opposite-type listings from other authors\nPrioritise normalised category compatibility\nExclude reserved, consumed and recovered listings\nApply date tolerance and revision-specific rejections
      DB --> Selector : Eligible projected candidates, possibly none
      Selector --> Matching : Candidate pool with listing revisions
      alt Candidate pool empty
        Matching -> Matching : Prepare ready result with an empty candidate list
      else Candidates available
        Matching -> Ranker : Rank source/candidate pairs\nusing versioned ranking configuration
        loop Each candidate pair
          Ranker -> Embeddings : Get available visual evidence for photo pair\nand compatible model/preprocessing versions
          Embeddings -> DB : Read cached embeddings by photo identity/revision,\nmodel version and preprocessing version
          DB --> Embeddings : Compatible vectors or missing/unavailable features
          alt Both photos have compatible normalised vectors
            Embeddings -> Embeddings : Compare vectors for visual similarity\nInitial proposed method: cosine similarity
            Embeddings --> Ranker : VisualScore with feature versions
          else Photo or usable embedding missing
            Embeddings --> Ranker : No visual score; explicit feature status
          end
          Ranker -> Ranker : Combine available category, colour, location,\ndate and optional visual evidence\nDerive reasons from the actual calculation
        end
        Ranker -> Ranker : Apply configured relevance threshold and sort\nKeep visual similarity distinct from total relevance
        Ranker --> Matching : Ranked candidate pool, revisions, scores,\nreasons and RankingVersion; possibly empty
      end
    end
    Matching --> Listings : Ready ranked pool or explicit processing outcome
    alt Ready result
      Listings -> Listings : Recheck source revision and eligibility\nagainst authoritative current data
      alt Source changed or became ineligible
        Listings --> Web : Refresh-required or current unavailable outcome
        Web --> User : Show current state and allow reload
      else Source still current and eligible
        Listings -> Listings : Recheck candidate revisions, Open state, reservations,\nconsumed/recovered links and pair rejections\nDiscard stale/ineligible results; take zero to three
        Listings --> Web : Current suggestions with supported reasons\nor a ready empty result
        Web --> User : Display relevance and optional visual similarity\nShow an empty state when no result remains
      end
    else Pending, failed or unavailable result
      Listings --> Web : Explicit processing status
      Web --> User : Show status and allow a later retry
    end
  end
end

note over Embeddings, DB
  DINOv3 extraction uses the local host through an authenticated tunnel
  with durable work and bounded concurrency, cached by photo/model/preprocessing version.
  A cache miss is not an instruction to infer every photo during this query.
  Local Qwen proposes editable traits in UC05; neither model confirms a match.
end note
note over User, Listings
  Viewing suggestions creates no acceptance, recovery or points.
  UC09 decisions and UC10 physical recovery are separate Listings operations.
  Relevance scores are not validated ownership probabilities.
end note
@enduml
